1
00:02:43,237 --> 00:02:44,505
Come to dinner.

2
00:02:48,957 --> 00:02:51,913
Come on, Mirandolina, eat that.

3
00:02:53,794 --> 00:02:54,870
You don't like it?

4
00:02:58,479 --> 00:03:01,780
Go on, eat...
That's all I have.

5
00:03:32,532 --> 00:03:34,875
So missy, I've got a headache.

6
00:03:37,677 --> 00:03:40,824
For about 4 days now
I have a headache and I throw up

7
00:03:41,592 --> 00:03:43,743
but I don't think it's from the stomach.

8
00:03:46,315 --> 00:03:47,581
No...

9
00:03:49,001 --> 00:03:53,455
Aspirin, algocalmin,
extraveral and distonocalm.

10
00:03:58,907 --> 00:04:02,323
No, I can't really, I've just
told you I've got a headache.

11
00:04:04,935 --> 00:04:08,621
Well, yeah, I drink,
like any other man.

12
00:04:11,652 --> 00:04:14,877
I had a little drink today, too...

13
00:04:16,758 --> 00:04:19,600
Not quite so, missy,
it's not like I'd drink any crap.

14
00:04:22,211 --> 00:04:24,169
Going on 63...

15
00:04:26,779 --> 00:04:30,388
2 Fetesti street, F4 building.

16
00:04:31,847 --> 00:04:35,494
Yeah, 2nd floor, flat 17.

17
00:04:37,759 --> 00:04:45,284
Lazarescu Dante Remus.

18
00:04:47,243 --> 00:04:49,968
Yes, I'm home.

19
00:04:51,657 --> 00:04:54,191
Thank you and I wish you good night.

20
00:05:32,889 --> 00:05:35,538
<i>In the sea
there are but predatory fish.</i>

21
00:05:35,845 --> 00:05:38,878
<i>You can use polenta for small fish.</i>

22
00:05:39,185 --> 00:05:42,219
<i>Here the big fish eats the small one.</i>

23
00:05:42,641 --> 00:05:46,557
<i>They're all on meat,
polenta doesn't really work in the sea.</i>

24
00:05:46,864 --> 00:05:49,782
<i>It is the wrong kind of bait.</i>

25
00:05:50,665 --> 00:05:53,391
<i>"Well", he said,
"I'm here for the salty air".</i>

26
00:05:53,621 --> 00:05:58,344
<i>The air works ok but if you don't
catch anything, know what I mean.</i>

27
00:05:58,843 --> 00:06:02,258
<i>If you don't get votes...
We didn't get any clear message.</i>

28
00:06:02,527 --> 00:06:04,409
<i>Once again, no message.</i>

29
00:06:04,754 --> 00:06:07,212
<i>Cause, look,
Ciuhandu an honorable character,</i>

30
00:06:07,404 --> 00:06:10,207
<i>flawless speech, serious.</i>

31
00:06:10,399 --> 00:06:13,700
<i>You'd expect him to rally
the people from Timisoara</i>

32
00:06:13,930 --> 00:06:16,579
<i>and get at least 90% of the votes.</i>

33
00:06:16,848 --> 00:06:19,958
<i>Timisoara turned out rather poor.</i>

34
00:06:37,272 --> 00:06:39,192
Hello, missy, it's me again.

35
00:06:40,574 --> 00:06:43,799
Hello, yes, the Ambulance.

36
00:06:44,951 --> 00:06:46,794
It's me again, Lazarescu.

37
00:06:49,404 --> 00:06:54,318
Then tell the colleague I spoke with
I had ulcer surgery 14 years ago

38
00:06:54,587 --> 00:07:00,614
and I also have leg ulcer
but no big deal.

39
00:07:02,611 --> 00:07:06,565
I've been thinking this headache
might be from the stomach.

40
00:07:07,486 --> 00:07:10,904
Lazarescu.
Fetesti 2.

41
00:07:13,475 --> 00:07:14,896
Ok, I got that.

42
00:07:15,703 --> 00:07:19,925
I don't think it's serious but
I rather get a specialist's opinion.

43
00:07:21,461 --> 00:07:23,266
Thank you
and I'll be waiting for you.

44
00:08:43,120 --> 00:08:45,002
My surgery is hurting, cat face.

45
00:08:47,688 --> 00:08:50,107
You don't care, you bloody animal.

46
00:09:43,510 --> 00:09:45,315
Compote.

47
00:10:20,866 --> 00:10:22,785
How you're doing Nusu?

48
00:10:23,744 --> 00:10:31,691
And you, the little one.
Where have you been wandering all day?

49
00:10:34,149 --> 00:10:39,101
You dogcat,
sit here nicely dogcat.

50
00:10:55,495 --> 00:10:56,685
Go to fuck.

51
00:11:03,517 --> 00:11:05,591
Just fucking close.

52
00:11:11,810 --> 00:11:14,307
Where are you going kitten?

53
00:11:21,716 --> 00:11:23,442
Madam de Pompadour.

54
00:11:24,979 --> 00:11:26,936
Incoerenza.

55
00:11:43,484 --> 00:11:51,085
...five-four-five.

56
00:11:55,731 --> 00:11:58,495
Hello, is this
the Muscalu residence? Virgil?

57
00:11:59,800 --> 00:12:03,562
Hi Virgil, how you're doing?
Is Eva there?

58
00:12:07,095 --> 00:12:09,935
Hold on man, I haven't forgotten.
Why do you think I've called?

59
00:12:12,354 --> 00:12:16,462
You, my sister, whatever.

60
00:12:17,653 --> 00:12:19,302
Hello, Virgil, Virgil.

61
00:12:19,878 --> 00:12:24,025
I've sent the money by post today
and you gonna get it tomorrow.

62
00:12:28,363 --> 00:12:32,318
Right, then next time I'll get
my pension I'll just send it all to you.

63
00:12:33,164 --> 00:12:35,004
That's better, isn't it?

64
00:12:37,462 --> 00:12:39,958
So, say,
can you put Eva on the phone?

65
00:12:41,647 --> 00:12:44,642
Well I said I'll send it by 1st,
and I did.

66
00:12:46,177 --> 00:12:49,209
Now can I speak with Eva?
Please!

67
00:12:51,052 --> 00:12:53,433
I'll wait, of course,
I'm not gonna run.

68
00:12:59,383 --> 00:13:01,726
Hey sis, how are you?

69
00:13:04,452 --> 00:13:08,137
That's just what I wanted
to talk with you about.

70
00:13:09,058 --> 00:13:13,896
Why didn't you tell me
you spoke with Bianca?

71
00:13:17,160 --> 00:13:21,958
Sure, you told me after I asked you.
You know very well I'm right.

72
00:13:22,803 --> 00:13:25,988
If she only calls you...

73
00:13:28,600 --> 00:13:31,595
I know damn well
that she calls you more often.

74
00:13:33,976 --> 00:13:37,544
Listen, I don't feel that well
with my ulcer.

75
00:13:38,965 --> 00:13:41,269
What's with you all,
talking about this drinking?

76
00:13:41,576 --> 00:13:43,496
You don't get ulcer from alcohol.

77
00:13:45,646 --> 00:13:48,985
I'm sorry, but I drink
at my own expense.

78
00:13:49,562 --> 00:13:51,673
Do you hear me Eva,
I drink at my own expense.

79
00:13:52,748 --> 00:13:56,396
You get ulcer from helico bacteria.

80
00:13:57,701 --> 00:13:59,966
Well, see,
you're learning new things.

81
00:14:01,655 --> 00:14:04,227
No Eva, I have no idea.

82
00:14:04,957 --> 00:14:08,987
I have this surgery for 14 years and
I haven't got a clue. Luckily you do.

83
00:14:10,332 --> 00:14:13,863
Good thing you, intellectuals,
know better than the doctors.

84
00:14:17,396 --> 00:14:21,235
Yeah, alright. But I'm asking you
nicely to stop lecturing me.

85
00:14:21,926 --> 00:14:25,457
Do you hear me Eva?
Stop lecturing and nagging me.

86
00:14:27,031 --> 00:14:29,873
No, you wouldn't like it either.

87
00:14:32,561 --> 00:14:33,789
I don't know.

88
00:14:34,826 --> 00:14:38,319
I don't know, but maybe
you don't want to speak with me anymore.

89
00:14:38,703 --> 00:14:41,850
I noticed that only Virgil
answers the phone lately.

90
00:14:44,807 --> 00:14:47,456
Ok, we'll do it the way you want.

91
00:14:52,217 --> 00:14:53,523
Thank you.

92
00:14:54,175 --> 00:14:57,169
And thank your sweet husband
for the money,

93
00:14:58,474 --> 00:15:01,276
Fine, and leave me with my ulcer

94
00:15:01,699 --> 00:15:06,384
and keep on talking to Bianca,
gossiping about my drinking.

95
00:15:07,919 --> 00:15:11,526
Ok you, but in the end I drink
at my own expense.

96
00:15:12,410 --> 00:15:15,136
Do you hear me Eva?
I drink at my own expense.

97
00:15:16,711 --> 00:15:18,169
Goodbye!

98
00:15:18,976 --> 00:15:20,089
Cheerio!

99
00:15:23,237 --> 00:15:24,964
Gracefully yours!

100
00:15:44,352 --> 00:15:45,850
Hello, yes.

101
00:16:35,835 --> 00:16:37,678
- My respects, ma'am.
- Yes, what is it?

102
00:16:38,447 --> 00:16:39,713
<i>Well done, you left with the mitts.</i>

103
00:16:40,097 --> 00:16:41,634
Just a second.

104
00:16:48,082 --> 00:16:50,309
Where on the balcony should I put it?
Cheers Romica!

105
00:16:50,846 --> 00:16:52,459
- Where should I take it?
- Take it to the balcony.

106
00:16:53,649 --> 00:16:56,951
Take it to the balcony and put it down,
on the tiles, by the plant.

107
00:17:25,015 --> 00:17:26,666
- Good evening.
- Evening dear.

108
00:17:28,394 --> 00:17:30,621
<i>Smaranda, tie your shoelaces, please.</i>

109
00:17:35,150 --> 00:17:37,492
What's wrong,
aren't you feeling very well?

110
00:17:42,292 --> 00:17:46,016
I beg your pardon Mrs. Mihaela,
so, I've called the ambulance,

111
00:17:46,285 --> 00:17:50,545
but until it arrives could you give me,
I mean lend me a Distonocalm?

112
00:17:51,851 --> 00:17:53,962
I don't know, I'll have a look,
but I don't think we got any.

113
00:17:55,115 --> 00:17:57,572
But if you've been drinking
your headache is from the alcohol.

114
00:17:59,184 --> 00:18:01,411
You drank, 'cause you smell.

115
00:18:02,332 --> 00:18:08,053
Lady, please be so kind
and have a look. I'll pay for them.

116
00:18:08,744 --> 00:18:11,431
C'mon now, let's be serious.
It's not about the money.

117
00:18:11,814 --> 00:18:15,577
I got this headache at the temple
before having the drink.

118
00:18:17,266 --> 00:18:19,110
I'm afraid we don't have
strong painkillers

119
00:18:19,378 --> 00:18:21,374
cause we don't buy such things.

120
00:18:24,100 --> 00:18:26,249
Ill go and look for a Distonocalm.

121
00:18:27,094 --> 00:18:30,781
What's up Romica? The stomach again
or it's moved on the pancreas?

122
00:18:32,240 --> 00:18:33,775
Stop drinking Romica.

123
00:18:35,349 --> 00:18:37,075
Let go of the fucking bottle.

124
00:18:39,264 --> 00:18:41,607
Stop drinking or you're going down.

125
00:18:42,106 --> 00:18:44,947
I threw up 4 times today,
from the aspirin.

126
00:18:46,521 --> 00:18:48,671
I don't think
I can stand it any longer, Sandu.

127
00:18:49,054 --> 00:18:50,821
What do you want me to bring you?

128
00:18:51,204 --> 00:18:53,469
A pill of Metoclopramide
or some cabbage juice?

129
00:18:53,777 --> 00:18:56,387
I've called the ambulance
and I thought of taking a pill.

130
00:18:56,925 --> 00:18:59,573
Ambulance on a Saturday?
You think they would bother?

131
00:19:00,649 --> 00:19:01,992
Screw them.

132
00:19:03,106 --> 00:19:05,909
They would rip you off
since they raised the medicines prices.

133
00:19:06,600 --> 00:19:10,516
<i>What you need is rest, buddy,
sohlaffen and cabbage juice.</i>

134
00:19:15,084 --> 00:19:17,273
Don't be tense,
it won't go away if you fight it.

135
00:19:17,542 --> 00:19:19,039
- It hurts, Sandu.
- Don't be stubborn.

136
00:19:28,943 --> 00:19:32,552
Like I said, I didn't find Distonocalm
but I brought you Diclofenac.

137
00:19:34,971 --> 00:19:37,006
But I have Diclofenac.

138
00:19:43,917 --> 00:19:45,797
Well, I don't know what to say,

139
00:19:46,603 --> 00:19:49,674
- Let me give you one just now.
- Don't rush to give him one.

140
00:19:50,366 --> 00:19:53,207
It isn't good for ulcer.
Check this out.

141
00:19:54,167 --> 00:19:57,584
- We only buy homeopathics for ourselves.
- So, do you need this?

142
00:19:58,543 --> 00:20:01,384
I'm not sure, I wanted a Distonocalm.

143
00:20:02,497 --> 00:20:04,801
And you give him Diclofenac when
the man's been puking since morning.

144
00:20:07,105 --> 00:20:10,330
I didn't know. I'll go
and get Metrocropmide right away.

145
00:20:11,173 --> 00:20:13,054
He should have said it's nausea.

146
00:20:14,130 --> 00:20:18,776
When I'm hung over, I just rub
my arms and I'm back to normal.

147
00:20:19,275 --> 00:20:20,466
What's she doing?

148
00:20:22,116 --> 00:20:23,728
<i>Oh, fuck!
Miki!</i>

149
00:20:24,995 --> 00:20:26,261
What?

150
00:20:26,607 --> 00:20:28,488
<i>What the hell are you doing,
trying to set us on fire?</i>

151
00:20:29,179 --> 00:20:34,363
<i>Wait, don't turn it off.
Turn it down and leave it.</i>

152
00:20:37,741 --> 00:20:39,162
<i>Come on, it didnt get burned.</i>

153
00:20:39,507 --> 00:20:41,887
<i>Nice of you to sort this one out.
Another one sorted by you!</i>

154
00:20:44,498 --> 00:20:46,801
Look at my burn. Fucking pan!

155
00:20:49,681 --> 00:20:51,332
Are you gonna get those pills?

156
00:20:55,785 --> 00:20:57,858
So, Romica, note the following aspect.

157
00:20:58,548 --> 00:21:03,310
the nausea is caused by the drink
and it's not good for your stomach.

158
00:21:04,308 --> 00:21:08,800
you don't drink the right way,
you're mixing the drinks.

159
00:21:10,183 --> 00:21:12,140
Stop mixing the drinks.

160
00:21:13,906 --> 00:21:18,091
Gee, but you stink. What the hell
have you drunk? Rat poison?

161
00:21:20,011 --> 00:21:21,969
Are you giving me that, or what?

162
00:21:23,926 --> 00:21:27,190
These are not good for you,
with your ulcer...

163
00:21:31,105 --> 00:21:32,757
Only after you eat.

164
00:21:33,333 --> 00:21:34,867
- How are you doing, boy?
- Good evening.

165
00:21:35,136 --> 00:21:39,052
Robert, tell your dad I need that
drilling machine if he's finished with it.

166
00:21:39,859 --> 00:21:43,085
Tell him to bring it down,
cause I need the fucking thing.

167
00:21:43,622 --> 00:21:46,079
- OK, Ill tell him.
- Don't forget.

168
00:21:46,999 --> 00:21:49,341
Great, I have to ask
for my own things!

169
00:21:50,378 --> 00:21:53,027
So, Romica, one for now

170
00:21:54,716 --> 00:21:57,635
and the other one for tomorrow
morning, with the coffee.

171
00:21:58,862 --> 00:22:02,086
But first, take a hot bath, eat
something, and then you take the pill.

172
00:22:02,587 --> 00:22:05,812
But get in the tub, and make sure
it's hot, otherwise it's useless.

173
00:22:06,733 --> 00:22:10,572
Come on, up a daisy.
You have to move, to sweat the alcohol.

174
00:22:15,870 --> 00:22:20,017
Listen, Sandu, I was feeling well,
and now I'm feeling ill.

175
00:22:20,592 --> 00:22:21,897
Let's take you to bed.

176
00:22:22,627 --> 00:22:27,656
I had this stomach ache from my ulcer,
and now I have a headache too.

177
00:22:28,232 --> 00:22:30,191
Now I have a headache
and a stomach ache.

178
00:22:31,572 --> 00:22:34,796
Easy buddy,
let me get you inside, to lie down.

179
00:22:36,448 --> 00:22:38,944
Wait, easy now.

180
00:22:39,481 --> 00:22:41,132
- I can manage.
- Sure.

181
00:22:51,881 --> 00:22:54,415
<i>Once again, the lack of concentration
leads to death on the Romanian roads.</i>

182
00:22:54,684 --> 00:22:56,796
<i>While driving on the national road 1,
a heavy truck driver fell asleep,</i>

183
00:22:56,988 --> 00:22:59,406
<i>and left his lane going over
to the other side of the road.</i>

184
00:22:59,675 --> 00:23:02,747
<i>He then hit a bus full of tourists,
just outside Saftica village.</i>

185
00:23:02,976 --> 00:23:04,857
<i>This collision has triggered
a chain crash.</i>

186
00:23:05,280 --> 00:23:10,195
<i>Up to now there are 7 recorded deaths
and 29 people in serious condition.</i>

187
00:23:13,880 --> 00:23:15,723
Were you watching this,
or is it better off?

188
00:23:16,030 --> 00:23:17,105
No.

189
00:23:19,677 --> 00:23:24,552
Listen, how long does it take for
a money order to get to Targu Mures?

190
00:23:28,276 --> 00:23:32,347
- I don't know... a few days.
- It's impossible.

191
00:23:33,422 --> 00:23:35,571
At the post office, they told me
it will be there tomorrow.

192
00:23:36,415 --> 00:23:38,335
No way. Tomorrow is Sunday.

193
00:23:40,485 --> 00:23:41,829
True.

194
00:23:46,359 --> 00:23:48,394
I think you should lie down and sleep.

195
00:23:52,962 --> 00:23:55,727
I can't sleep.
I don't feel like sleeping

196
00:23:56,802 --> 00:23:59,604
What is she doing with that pill,
inventing it?

197
00:24:20,605 --> 00:24:22,792
Oh dear,
the smell of cat hair in here.

198
00:24:25,480 --> 00:24:27,361
How is it Mr. engineer,
still not asleep?

199
00:24:30,394 --> 00:24:31,700
Go on, give me your glasses.

200
00:24:32,276 --> 00:24:34,771
Yes, very well,
so he won't break them.

201
00:24:36,191 --> 00:24:37,880
Can you get us a glass of water now?

202
00:24:48,976 --> 00:24:51,625
Look how dirty it is,
and they're all the same.

203
00:24:51,933 --> 00:24:54,658
- Should I bring a clean one from us?
- And what else, Miki?

204
00:24:55,042 --> 00:24:57,422
Just go on and pour some water in it,
so we can give him that pill.

205
00:25:00,147 --> 00:25:03,526
My oh my, you should be sent
to fetch the Death.

206
00:25:05,600 --> 00:25:07,250
You know what they say:

207
00:25:07,904 --> 00:25:10,935
"Mascara doesn't help you
if you don't know how to speak".

208
00:25:12,816 --> 00:25:15,121
"Doesn't help
if you have no manners. "

209
00:25:15,620 --> 00:25:17,578
I think the pain is from the aspirin.

210
00:25:19,421 --> 00:25:20,957
Do you like quince jelly?

211
00:25:22,492 --> 00:25:24,373
I feel kind of droopy.

212
00:25:25,678 --> 00:25:27,367
Aren't you better lying down?

213
00:25:28,212 --> 00:25:30,554
After a good sleep,
youll be as good as new.

214
00:25:31,361 --> 00:25:32,819
Move over just a bit.

215
00:25:35,007 --> 00:25:37,772
- Come on here and see your "nothing".
- What do you mean?

216
00:25:38,118 --> 00:25:39,922
You said my finger is alright.

217
00:25:40,458 --> 00:25:43,031
Have a closer look, to see better.

218
00:25:44,721 --> 00:25:47,677
See, it's swollen already,
don't pretend you can't see.

219
00:25:48,060 --> 00:25:49,634
Yes, it seems a bit swollen.

220
00:25:50,287 --> 00:25:55,049
Come on, get up.
You should finish what you start.

221
00:25:56,353 --> 00:25:58,694
You just don't leave
the pan and go away

222
00:25:59,040 --> 00:26:02,611
cause, look, I ruined my fingers
and the stuff got burned.

223
00:26:04,339 --> 00:26:06,373
It's not burned, I've tasted it.

224
00:26:06,911 --> 00:26:10,597
Come on, get up, this is for nausea.
Put your tongue out.

225
00:26:11,748 --> 00:26:14,282
But he can't take Diclofenac
on an empty stomach.

226
00:26:14,781 --> 00:26:17,315
- He should eat before taking it.
- What do you think you're doing?

227
00:26:20,656 --> 00:26:24,418
Leave us already with your kindness.
Leave him alone to swallow his pill.

228
00:26:30,214 --> 00:26:31,942
You won't feel the effect right away,

229
00:26:32,172 --> 00:26:34,783
but don't worry, in about 20 minutes
it's gonna go away.

230
00:26:36,740 --> 00:26:39,083
Here, take this glass to the kitchen

231
00:26:39,582 --> 00:26:43,729
and go check on that pot,
so we won't get anymore surprises.

232
00:26:44,343 --> 00:26:46,683
Don't worry, I turned down the heat.

233
00:26:51,752 --> 00:26:54,248
I don't know why aren't you
getting rid of these cats?

234
00:26:54,517 --> 00:26:57,627
- Why don't you get rid of Miki?
- What do you mean?

235
00:26:58,317 --> 00:27:01,196
- Why don't you get rid of your wife?
- Why, is it the same thing?

236
00:27:01,772 --> 00:27:04,114
I don't know, is it the same thing?

237
00:27:06,956 --> 00:27:10,142
These cats, they're gonna kill you
with their hair and their fleas.

238
00:27:11,831 --> 00:27:15,401
Mark my words.
We'll see who was right in the end.

239
00:27:18,089 --> 00:27:20,585
How nice and cozy you must feel
now that you found your fool.

240
00:27:22,119 --> 00:27:24,385
They sleep all day
and leave hair everywhere.

241
00:27:25,920 --> 00:27:28,071
Look how it stinks in here.

242
00:27:31,411 --> 00:27:35,403
Should I bring him a bit of moussaka?
There's nothing in his fridge.

243
00:27:36,594 --> 00:27:39,818
- No Mrs. Mihaela, please don't.
- It's very tasty.

244
00:27:40,241 --> 00:27:43,043
- I'm not eating.
- I made it with pork not with beef.

245
00:27:44,503 --> 00:27:46,382
What is it Miki, what do you want?

246
00:27:46,805 --> 00:27:48,993
Weren't you saying
he should take that pill?

247
00:27:49,569 --> 00:27:51,566
And he has nothing to eat.
Cooked, I mean.

248
00:27:52,180 --> 00:27:53,563
So?

249
00:27:53,832 --> 00:27:55,521
I thought of bringing some moussaka,

250
00:27:55,713 --> 00:27:58,054
so he won't take the pill
on an empty stomach.

251
00:27:58,515 --> 00:28:02,699
- Miki, will you go watch that jelly?
- Alright.

252
00:28:09,073 --> 00:28:11,376
See what I get if I let her talk?

253
00:28:13,565 --> 00:28:15,100
And these newspapers...

254
00:28:15,638 --> 00:28:20,130
Why don't you bin them and clean up.
All this paper just gathers dust.

255
00:28:37,175 --> 00:28:39,902
Romica, this is not good.

256
00:28:41,552 --> 00:28:44,854
I think we should call the ambulance,
'cause look you threw up blood vines.

257
00:28:49,883 --> 00:28:51,188
Hold on.

258
00:28:55,795 --> 00:28:57,063
<i>Come on quick.</i>

259
00:29:05,738 --> 00:29:09,540
Look. Exactly like mine
when I had that Malory-Weiss disease.

260
00:29:11,075 --> 00:29:17,487
Yeah, but yours had more blood in it.
And it had bits from those sausages.

261
00:29:19,945 --> 00:29:22,899
- This looks more watery.
- It's secretion from my stomach.

262
00:29:23,629 --> 00:29:26,931
You stained your slippers.
I'll go wash them.

263
00:29:46,894 --> 00:29:48,315
What is it?

264
00:29:49,621 --> 00:29:52,922
- I say we call for the ambulance.
- He's already called the ambulance.

265
00:29:53,882 --> 00:29:55,955
You called it, haven't you?

266
00:29:56,570 --> 00:30:00,101
I know that, but don't you know
it takes them forever to get here?

267
00:30:10,581 --> 00:30:13,231
- Romica, where's that phone?
- It's in the kitchen.

268
00:30:18,414 --> 00:30:20,987
Don't worry, Malory-Weiss
sounds worse than it really is.

269
00:30:23,788 --> 00:30:26,323
- It's the ulcer Mrs. Mihaela.
- What are you saying?

270
00:30:26,745 --> 00:30:28,319
It's from the ulcer.

271
00:30:29,164 --> 00:30:31,889
Sure, Sandu had an endoscopy
and he's been cauterized.

272
00:30:33,157 --> 00:30:36,727
<i>Yes, he's my next door neighbor.</i>

273
00:30:40,335 --> 00:30:44,520
<i>About 60, actually over 60,
cause he's older than me.</i>

274
00:30:46,286 --> 00:30:50,932
<i>So, he has a headache
and he keeps throwing up blood.</i>

275
00:30:54,042 --> 00:30:59,262
<i>Yes, that's right, he drinks a bit.
I keep telling him not to...</i>

276
00:31:10,089 --> 00:31:12,776
They should be here any minute.
They're on their way. The ambulance.

277
00:31:14,235 --> 00:31:17,460
Come on, take a hike,
you slept enough.

278
00:31:21,338 --> 00:31:22,950
Go and see who's ringing.

279
00:31:25,984 --> 00:31:28,709
There's no need to be afraid
of Malory-Weiss, it's no big deal.

280
00:31:29,323 --> 00:31:31,204
They will cauterize it
through an endoscopy.

281
00:31:31,935 --> 00:31:35,389
But you know how it is, you had
endoscopy for your ulcer, didn't you?

282
00:31:36,195 --> 00:31:39,229
The pain is moving about.
The ulcer.

283
00:31:44,526 --> 00:31:46,599
It's Mr. Gelu, he brought
your drilling machine.

284
00:31:51,553 --> 00:31:54,201
How you're doing Romica,
lost the compass?

285
00:31:54,623 --> 00:31:57,120
- Don't laugh, it's not funny at all.
- He threw up blood.

286
00:31:58,846 --> 00:32:00,420
What does this mean?
Is it serious?

287
00:32:00,688 --> 00:32:02,570
What does it mean,
what does it mean... it just means.

288
00:32:02,801 --> 00:32:05,834
- Are we talking hospital here?
- No, we're talking carnival.

289
00:32:06,871 --> 00:32:08,829
Yes it's serious,
we called the Ambulance.

290
00:32:09,826 --> 00:32:12,706
- Let's check if it has all the bits.
- Great, thanks for the trust.

291
00:32:14,625 --> 00:32:16,890
I thought I could forget about it.

292
00:32:17,658 --> 00:32:19,847
I thought
it's in the flea market already.

293
00:32:27,602 --> 00:32:29,598
Take it and put it on my desk.

294
00:32:32,938 --> 00:32:36,892
Then you stay here with Mr. Lazarescu.
I have to pour the jelly into jars, OK?

295
00:32:43,228 --> 00:32:46,144
Say, are we still on
for the booze trip?

296
00:32:46,643 --> 00:32:49,139
I spoke with the guy, and he'd be
waiting for us next Saturday.

297
00:32:49,523 --> 00:32:52,556
We leave Saturday morning
and we'll be back by evening.

298
00:32:53,938 --> 00:32:56,703
What about the double-glazing?
You're still getting them?

299
00:32:56,972 --> 00:32:58,239
Winter is close.

300
00:32:58,546 --> 00:33:00,542
Don't think so.
Maybe next year, in the spring.

301
00:33:00,888 --> 00:33:02,192
So tell me, what's it gonna be?

302
00:33:02,499 --> 00:33:05,264
Let me pass,
I have to go to the bathroom.

303
00:33:07,222 --> 00:33:08,643
Can you handle it?

304
00:33:09,832 --> 00:33:13,173
Look at him going. Call the ambulance,
tell them not to bother,

305
00:33:13,403 --> 00:33:15,707
Lazarescu
is "mensana in corpore sana".

306
00:33:19,354 --> 00:33:23,691
I told the guy to save some white
and some red. Grasa and Cabernet.

307
00:33:25,343 --> 00:33:27,224
I don't know what to say,
I'm kind of short with the money.

308
00:33:27,570 --> 00:33:29,873
It's 100 kilos. 50 and 50.

309
00:33:30,219 --> 00:33:34,595
I don't know, I spent a lot on potatoes
and pickles. I'm almost skint.

310
00:33:36,092 --> 00:33:37,705
Well, why don't you ask your son?

311
00:33:37,974 --> 00:33:39,586
He doesn't have either,
they have their own problems.

312
00:33:39,816 --> 00:33:41,545
Doinita has been on maternity leave
for a month now.

313
00:33:41,736 --> 00:33:44,002
He wants to change his job.
They have no money.

314
00:33:44,885 --> 00:33:48,454
You mother fucking pervert
now you really pissed me off!

315
00:33:49,030 --> 00:33:50,451
Wait 'till I get my hands on you.

316
00:33:50,873 --> 00:33:52,677
Where are you? Come over here.

317
00:33:54,943 --> 00:33:57,094
I'll shut you up in an instant.

318
00:33:59,281 --> 00:34:00,664
Get in here.

319
00:34:08,802 --> 00:34:11,297
I've never seen as much filth
as in this man's flat.

320
00:34:11,912 --> 00:34:14,484
Look at the dirt on those papers.

321
00:34:20,089 --> 00:34:21,663
What would you expect
from normal folk

322
00:34:21,931 --> 00:34:23,851
if an intellectual
lives with his cats?

323
00:34:24,965 --> 00:34:27,538
I could lend you some money
till after Christmas.

324
00:34:27,921 --> 00:34:29,188
<i>Sandu I</i>

325
00:34:29,649 --> 00:34:31,262
Listen to that one screaming.

326
00:34:31,991 --> 00:34:34,371
And his daughter didn't give a fuck.
and left for America.

327
00:34:34,601 --> 00:34:35,675
- Canada.
- What?

328
00:34:36,021 --> 00:34:37,327
Bianca went to Canada.

329
00:34:37,596 --> 00:34:40,475
America, Canada, screw the bitch that
leaves her old man alone.

330
00:34:41,397 --> 00:34:42,779
God forgive me.

331
00:34:44,814 --> 00:34:46,233
I think they're here.

332
00:34:51,109 --> 00:34:52,875
- Good evening madam.
- Good evening. Mr. Lazarescu?

333
00:34:53,182 --> 00:34:55,717
No, I'm the next door neighbor,
I'm the one who called you, Sterian.

334
00:34:56,484 --> 00:34:57,789
- Good evening.
- Hello.

335
00:34:58,212 --> 00:35:00,247
No, it's not him,
yours is in the bathroom.

336
00:35:00,669 --> 00:35:02,781
Come on Romica, hurry up,
the lady from the ambulance is here.

337
00:35:03,703 --> 00:35:05,046
Have a sit.

338
00:35:06,083 --> 00:35:07,772
Well then, should I go on my own?

339
00:35:08,079 --> 00:35:09,883
Let me solve this man's problem, first.

340
00:35:10,228 --> 00:35:13,185
- Then come up when you're done.
- Alright, see you.

341
00:35:14,183 --> 00:35:15,834
Come on, the ambulance is here.

342
00:35:16,448 --> 00:35:17,370
- Good evening.
- Good-bye.

343
00:35:19,596 --> 00:35:21,900
Gee, how did you get in there, man?

344
00:35:22,283 --> 00:35:24,318
- Come on up, easy.
- Easy, easy,

345
00:35:25,968 --> 00:35:29,463
- Can you use your legs?
- It's OK, nothing happened.

346
00:35:30,692 --> 00:35:34,339
- But can you stand up, can you walk?
- I've called for you.

347
00:35:34,799 --> 00:35:38,101
Are you hurt?
When you fell, did you hurt yourself?

348
00:35:38,561 --> 00:35:42,477
Good evening ma'am!
Sandu help me out, I can't use my legs.

349
00:35:43,630 --> 00:35:47,660
- Come on up, nice and easy.
- Show the lady you're OK,

350
00:35:48,965 --> 00:35:50,924
My legs are OK miss.

351
00:35:52,344 --> 00:35:57,105
It's my belly that hurts.
My stomach and my white hair.

352
00:35:59,254 --> 00:36:01,328
We'll see what's wrong
in an instant.

353
00:36:04,553 --> 00:36:05,858
You had a drink, didn't you?

354
00:36:06,397 --> 00:36:09,237
Well yes,
I've drunk about a meter of spirits.

355
00:36:09,774 --> 00:36:13,459
- I see. And what is it that you drank?
- Mastropol.

356
00:36:15,110 --> 00:36:17,875
- What did you say its name was?
- Mas-tro-pol.

357
00:36:18,719 --> 00:36:21,139
It's a drink made by us
from double strength alcohol,

358
00:36:21,483 --> 00:36:25,169
burned sugar and a sachet of vanilla.
But there are no chemicals in it.

359
00:36:25,859 --> 00:36:27,894
Mastropol

360
00:36:30,928 --> 00:36:32,848
Now I would ask you to stay still.

361
00:36:35,189 --> 00:36:37,109
Calm and breathe normally.

362
00:36:38,107 --> 00:36:41,256
- Not like this, relax your chest.
- I know, I was just testing you.

363
00:36:41,946 --> 00:36:46,399
Yeah? You wanted to see
if I know my job.

364
00:36:51,045 --> 00:36:52,427
You're laughing...

365
00:37:09,014 --> 00:37:11,508
10 over 6... rather small.

366
00:37:14,195 --> 00:37:17,881
- See, this is Mastropol.
- And you drank all of this?

367
00:37:20,722 --> 00:37:22,258
How much of this Mastrapol
have you drunk?

368
00:37:22,833 --> 00:37:26,596
You have, cause you see,
you can't really use your legs.

369
00:37:27,940 --> 00:37:30,895
My surgery hurts,
that's why I've called you,

370
00:37:31,548 --> 00:37:32,969
What surgery?

371
00:37:33,659 --> 00:37:37,384
I have a perforated duodenal
ulcer surgery, nurse.

372
00:37:38,650 --> 00:37:40,110
- Perforated ulcer.
- Yes.

373
00:37:41,722 --> 00:37:45,138
I'll give you some vitamins and glucose
and you're gonna feel better.

374
00:37:46,367 --> 00:37:48,632
- Lazarescu Dante Remus.
- Lazarescu Dante Remus.

375
00:37:49,899 --> 00:37:53,009
- 63 years old.
- 63 next month, November the 19th.

376
00:37:54,315 --> 00:37:56,350
I don't know much about this,
but he threw up blood,

377
00:37:56,542 --> 00:37:58,422
and I thought
it might be from the stomach.

378
00:37:58,960 --> 00:38:04,296
Of course, having health problems and
drinking, sure leads to throwing up.

379
00:38:06,216 --> 00:38:08,442
I got Malory-Weiss
from drinking last year,

380
00:38:08,712 --> 00:38:10,784
and they cauterized it by endoscope.

381
00:38:11,245 --> 00:38:14,547
That's different.
Probably you had an accident.

382
00:38:16,005 --> 00:38:19,001
- No, I threw up from the effort.
- I have a stomach ache miss.

383
00:38:19,615 --> 00:38:22,916
My surgery hurts and I've been
throwing up since this morning.

384
00:38:23,415 --> 00:38:26,986
You threw up and your stomach hurts?
Then I'll give you an antacid.

385
00:38:29,405 --> 00:38:34,433
Tomorrow, after you'll feel better,
I mean the day after tomorrow, Monday,

386
00:38:34,740 --> 00:38:38,195
go see the doctor
that performed the surgery.

387
00:38:39,310 --> 00:38:42,497
I've been operated 14 years ago by
dr. Olteanu Vladimir, at the Municipal.

388
00:38:42,919 --> 00:38:46,105
Right, Municipal Hospital.
Now it's called Universitar.

389
00:38:47,409 --> 00:38:48,945
Just go see him.

390
00:38:49,828 --> 00:38:53,591
- My head hurts at the temples.
- Does it hurt really bad?

391
00:38:54,244 --> 00:38:56,624
- It hurts since morning.
- This morning.

392
00:38:58,582 --> 00:39:00,770
Then I'll give you a painkiller, too.

393
00:39:08,795 --> 00:39:10,598
You had this done this before,
hadn't you?

394
00:39:10,905 --> 00:39:11,750
Yes.

395
00:39:30,294 --> 00:39:31,561
Easy...

396
00:39:33,825 --> 00:39:35,207
It's not gonna hurt.

397
00:39:41,081 --> 00:39:44,383
- Look, they're here. Good evening.
- Good evening, ma'am.

398
00:39:47,262 --> 00:39:49,144
I brought him some moussaka from us.

399
00:39:49,566 --> 00:39:51,024
What do you say,
should I put it in the fridge

400
00:39:51,217 --> 00:39:53,059
or should I give him
a little right now?

401
00:39:55,479 --> 00:39:58,012
Mr. Lazarescu,
would you care to have some?

402
00:39:58,434 --> 00:40:00,008
Please leave him alone now.

403
00:40:05,115 --> 00:40:06,727
She is my wife.

404
00:40:07,494 --> 00:40:09,874
Hold on tight, like this. Press.

405
00:40:12,793 --> 00:40:15,481
I gave you this injection
because you drank.

406
00:40:21,431 --> 00:40:23,465
- I'll throw those away.
- Yes, thank you.

407
00:40:39,513 --> 00:40:41,779
You were saying
your stomach is aching.

408
00:40:43,199 --> 00:40:46,385
- Are you having bloody stools?
- I have runny stools.

409
00:40:47,845 --> 00:40:49,188
Almost like water.

410
00:40:51,953 --> 00:40:54,371
- Ouch, it hurts.
- Here?

411
00:40:54,947 --> 00:40:56,137
Ouch, yes.

412
00:40:57,596 --> 00:40:59,784
- Ouch, ouch.
- Does it hurt here?

413
00:41:00,667 --> 00:41:04,046
Can't you see I had surgery?
Don't you want to see certain things?

414
00:41:04,430 --> 00:41:06,004
- OK, OK, I got that.
- Calm down.

415
00:41:06,541 --> 00:41:07,579
I apologize

416
00:41:10,494 --> 00:41:14,258
Have you noticed any blood traces?
Or if the stool is black?

417
00:41:14,680 --> 00:41:18,597
It's not melena miss, don't insist.
I only have diarrhea. And I have cramps.

418
00:41:21,130 --> 00:41:24,471
You're saying it's not melena.
Do you eat normally?

419
00:41:25,967 --> 00:41:29,000
I eat, yes.
Cold cuts and cheese.

420
00:41:32,379 --> 00:41:35,373
Have you noticed losing weight
over the last month or week?

421
00:41:36,256 --> 00:41:38,752
- About two holes in my belt.
- How did you say?

422
00:41:39,750 --> 00:41:42,744
Yes, I lost weight,
about 2 holes in my belt.

423
00:41:44,972 --> 00:41:46,314
Yes, I see.

424
00:41:48,657 --> 00:41:51,805
- Is there someone else living with you?
- No, he lives alone.

425
00:41:52,458 --> 00:41:56,104
I live with three cats in a building
with neighbors that don't love animals.

426
00:41:57,179 --> 00:41:59,674
How could we love them
if they have fleas?

427
00:42:03,168 --> 00:42:05,856
You'll have to come with me
to be seen by a specialist.

428
00:42:07,853 --> 00:42:10,272
I'm gonna take your temperature,
and then we'll go.

429
00:42:15,799 --> 00:42:18,218
Have you ever been seen
by a colon specialist?

430
00:42:18,564 --> 00:42:20,254
There's nothing wrong with my colon.

431
00:42:23,670 --> 00:42:25,091
OK.

432
00:42:28,545 --> 00:42:32,231
I'm gonna have a cigarette
in the kitchen. Is smoking allowed?

433
00:42:32,730 --> 00:42:35,264
Yes, it is. Smoking, drinking,
all the sins.

434
00:42:39,027 --> 00:42:42,060
- Would you come with me?
- Sure.

435
00:42:48,662 --> 00:42:50,391
Don't worry, it will go away.

436
00:42:53,347 --> 00:42:56,034
No shit,
this is an astronaut's temperature.

437
00:42:59,027 --> 00:43:00,794
I know he has a sister in Targu Mures

438
00:43:01,101 --> 00:43:04,288
and a daughter, Bianca,
but she's emigrated to America.

439
00:43:04,595 --> 00:43:08,051
- And the wife?
- No, his wife died about 10 years ago.

440
00:43:08,550 --> 00:43:10,201
- I see.
- 8 years.

441
00:43:11,352 --> 00:43:12,273
Just a second.

442
00:43:14,424 --> 00:43:16,112
I brought him some moussaka.

443
00:43:18,723 --> 00:43:22,831
And could you come with us?
It would be easier if he's accompanied.

444
00:43:23,945 --> 00:43:26,825
I don't know, if you'd ask me
I would bother and come.

445
00:43:27,362 --> 00:43:30,319
But Sandu won't agree.
Sure, he is our neighbor.

446
00:43:31,508 --> 00:43:33,350
You'd help me with the admittance.

447
00:43:35,039 --> 00:43:36,729
Just between us women:

448
00:43:37,151 --> 00:43:39,839
I'm not happy with the friendship
between Lazarescu and my husband.

449
00:43:40,108 --> 00:43:42,066
He got Sandu into drinking.

450
00:43:42,373 --> 00:43:45,213
Before Lazarescus moved here,
Sandu didn't touch alcohol.

451
00:43:45,482 --> 00:43:48,169
Lazarescu taught him to drink
like they do in Hungary.

452
00:43:50,281 --> 00:43:52,431
But Lazarescu
is not a Hungarian name.

453
00:43:52,892 --> 00:43:56,195
No, he is Romanian.
But his wife, Erji, was Hungarian.

454
00:43:56,655 --> 00:43:58,535
The arrogant type.

455
00:44:00,148 --> 00:44:02,835
It wasn't us that put the bottle
in his hand

456
00:44:03,104 --> 00:44:07,212
and look at the filth he lives in
with these cats that soil the stairway.

457
00:44:08,326 --> 00:44:10,821
We live in the city, after all.

458
00:44:11,473 --> 00:44:13,662
- That's true.
- Of course I am right.

459
00:44:14,391 --> 00:44:16,772
And there's another one,
Dinescu, on the 4th floor.

460
00:44:17,079 --> 00:44:19,651
That one has a son that plays
the violin. He's been driving us crazy.

461
00:44:20,803 --> 00:44:24,948
At some point somebody has to take care
of these cats and throw them away.

462
00:44:28,135 --> 00:44:29,902
So your husband wouldn't go either.

463
00:44:30,209 --> 00:44:32,667
That'll be just great.
Of course he wouldn't.

464
00:44:33,127 --> 00:44:35,506
But I don't know, you should ask him.

465
00:44:36,121 --> 00:44:39,308
Please don't get me wrong.
We have a drink now and then

466
00:44:39,576 --> 00:44:42,418
but only at home,
where nobody can see us.

467
00:44:42,725 --> 00:44:46,295
And when you need a bit of help
he wouldn't give you a dime.

468
00:44:46,832 --> 00:44:49,596
And it's not that he wouldn't want to
but he doesn't have a thing.

469
00:44:50,287 --> 00:44:52,130
But what's wrong with him?
Is it serious?

470
00:44:52,476 --> 00:44:55,740
I'm only a nurse, I can't say for sure,
but it could be serious.

471
00:44:56,776 --> 00:45:00,116
Looks like a colon tumor,
but maybe I'm wrong.

472
00:45:01,075 --> 00:45:04,224
That's right.
His wife died of cancer too.

473
00:45:05,336 --> 00:45:06,873
It's not really necessary
to come with us,

474
00:45:07,065 --> 00:45:09,137
but it would have been
easier for me.

475
00:45:09,560 --> 00:45:11,364
In any case,
maybe you could call his sister,

476
00:45:11,556 --> 00:45:13,668
to come and see him in the hospital.

477
00:45:14,013 --> 00:45:15,473
What is it about?

478
00:45:15,780 --> 00:45:17,776
She was asking if we could go
with her to the hospital,

479
00:45:17,968 --> 00:45:19,735
for Lazarescu's admittance.

480
00:45:19,965 --> 00:45:22,574
- Just one of you.
- I said you wouldn't go.

481
00:45:23,841 --> 00:45:26,107
Usually it's easier for us
at the admittance

482
00:45:26,337 --> 00:45:28,410
if the patient comes attended.

483
00:45:30,944 --> 00:45:33,286
- Is it that serious?
- Yes, he has cancer.

484
00:45:34,130 --> 00:45:37,547
I didn't say that. But they'll
keep him at the hospital, for sure.

485
00:45:38,623 --> 00:45:43,307
He needs to have full tests done.
I only said he might have cancer.

486
00:45:49,104 --> 00:45:51,484
You mean from the ulcer?

487
00:45:51,907 --> 00:45:55,515
No, I reckon it's the colon
but it's better to see a doctor.

488
00:45:57,242 --> 00:45:59,738
- Say, Miki, should I go with the lady?
- I don't know.

489
00:46:00,774 --> 00:46:03,769
If they find something and keep him
there, will you walk home?

490
00:46:05,229 --> 00:46:08,607
Didn't I say that I'll call his sister?
Really now, I thought we agreed.

491
00:46:12,023 --> 00:46:14,249
Yeah, well, I'm sorry.

492
00:46:17,360 --> 00:46:18,512
Just a second.

493
00:46:22,850 --> 00:46:25,268
Thanks for leaving me alone
on a Saturday night.

494
00:46:29,492 --> 00:46:31,949
- How is it?
- 36 over 6, over 7.

495
00:46:32,333 --> 00:46:34,290
I have to get him to the hospital.

496
00:46:35,058 --> 00:46:37,362
We have to go to the hospital
Mr. Lazarescu.

497
00:46:37,861 --> 00:46:40,816
- Can you walk to the ambulance?
- Course I can.

498
00:46:42,007 --> 00:46:44,464
But first I'd like to call
my sister in Targu Mures.

499
00:46:46,153 --> 00:46:48,419
I'll do it, if you give me the number.

500
00:46:48,764 --> 00:46:49,762
- Yes?
- Yes.

501
00:46:50,952 --> 00:46:54,754
0265.

502
00:46:55,406 --> 00:46:56,863
- Area code
- Yes.

503
00:46:57,362 --> 00:46:59,667
- 0265,..
- Say again.

504
00:47:00,089 --> 00:47:02,239
- 263,
- 545.

505
00:47:04,120 --> 00:47:07,077
Thanks.
Sure I can.

506
00:47:08,268 --> 00:47:10,647
- Can you help me take him to the car?
- Sure.

507
00:47:11,376 --> 00:47:13,679
Take a pajama with you.
And some slippers.

508
00:47:14,717 --> 00:47:17,212
Then he needs a bag or something.

509
00:47:23,930 --> 00:47:27,423
<i>Hello, Mrs. Eva?
Miki Sterian speaking.</i>

510
00:47:28,115 --> 00:47:30,265
- Try to stand up. Need help?
- No, no.

511
00:47:31,533 --> 00:47:33,912
- Is this one Ok?
- Of course.

512
00:47:34,527 --> 00:47:36,446
- Are you putting this on?
- Yes.

513
00:47:40,593 --> 00:47:42,397
<i>They don't know, he needs a biopsy.</i>

514
00:47:43,088 --> 00:47:45,736
Don't push yourself. Ill help you.

515
00:47:48,232 --> 00:47:51,995
<i>I called to let you know they're taking
him to the hospital right now.</i>

516
00:47:52,226 --> 00:47:53,607
<i>The ambulance.</i>

517
00:47:59,903 --> 00:48:01,324
Mrs. Eva...

518
00:48:05,240 --> 00:48:06,968
Hi, yes.

519
00:48:09,923 --> 00:48:15,030
They are taking me to the hospital.
Don't worry, it's not serious.

520
00:48:17,026 --> 00:48:19,982
Come on, you're not going
to travel alone by night.

521
00:48:21,287 --> 00:48:24,513
- Can I speak with her for a moment?
- Hold on, let me put someone else on.

522
00:48:25,664 --> 00:48:27,777
Hello, good evening lady.

523
00:48:28,890 --> 00:48:32,037
I am the paramedic.
My name is Mioara Avram.

524
00:48:34,763 --> 00:48:37,374
Yes, the ER at St. Spiridon,
if you know where it is.

525
00:48:41,828 --> 00:48:43,747
I think it is.

526
00:48:45,358 --> 00:48:47,086
Yes I think you should come.

527
00:48:49,505 --> 00:48:52,155
- If you get here tomorrow, it's Ok.
- You're sitting in that puke.

528
00:48:54,766 --> 00:48:58,720
And if he won't be at the hospital,
he will be home. Yes, yes, thank you.

529
00:48:59,526 --> 00:49:00,717
Good evening.

530
00:49:01,138 --> 00:49:04,632
- What did she say, is she coming?
- Yes, she is. She'll be here tomorrow.

531
00:49:05,208 --> 00:49:07,166
- So it's settled.
- Of course it's settled.

532
00:49:07,742 --> 00:49:10,044
If the woman said she'll be here,
shell be here.

533
00:49:11,427 --> 00:49:14,537
Come on, easy, don't rush.

534
00:49:21,485 --> 00:49:23,674
Come on Romica,
the lady is waiting for you.

535
00:49:24,173 --> 00:49:26,438
It's stuck,
Here. There you are.

536
00:49:27,130 --> 00:49:29,318
- Ready.
- Sandu, would you lock the door?

537
00:49:29,510 --> 00:49:31,967
- I will, where's the key?
- There, on the fridge.

538
00:49:32,427 --> 00:49:33,617
Let me do it.

539
00:49:39,491 --> 00:49:42,525
- Where could those cats be?
- I took them to the bedroom.

540
00:49:43,562 --> 00:49:46,825
They're gonna ruin my flowers,
they'll make a mess.

541
00:49:48,282 --> 00:49:50,010
- Watch the stairs!
- Which lock?

542
00:49:50,548 --> 00:49:52,736
- The lower one.
- Pay attention, please.

543
00:49:53,120 --> 00:49:54,848
- Lean on me.
- Easy, there's no rush.

544
00:49:56,844 --> 00:50:02,219
Listen Sandu, if theyll keep me at
the hospital, feed my animals, will you?

545
00:50:04,868 --> 00:50:08,055
- Mirandolina, and Nusu and Fritz.
- I will, no problem.

546
00:50:09,743 --> 00:50:14,006
- Allow me. Let me help you.
- There's no need, I can manage.

547
00:50:15,311 --> 00:50:16,771
Let me, please.

548
00:50:20,033 --> 00:50:25,139
- Bones, fish, they're not demanding.
- Don't worry Romica, I'll feed them.

549
00:50:27,788 --> 00:50:30,169
Easy, up.

550
00:50:30,975 --> 00:50:33,662
- But only if they keep me at the hospital.
- Alright.

551
00:50:37,654 --> 00:50:39,036
Yes, what is it?

552
00:50:39,266 --> 00:50:41,571
My husband is bringing him downstairs
so that you'll take him to the hospital.

553
00:50:41,801 --> 00:50:43,491
I'll call you later,
I've got things to do.

554
00:50:43,990 --> 00:50:47,637
Come on already mom, I'm not Geanina
Yes, I got that, bye.

555
00:50:49,057 --> 00:50:50,325
Where is Mrs. Mioara?

556
00:50:50,555 --> 00:50:52,358
She's coming downstairs
with my husband.

557
00:51:00,498 --> 00:51:05,758
It's OK, leave us, we can manage.
Easy now Romica, we're here.

558
00:51:07,715 --> 00:51:11,016
- I can't fit into this, madam.
- Come on. What did you expect, a Mazda?

559
00:51:11,592 --> 00:51:13,052
Come on please, get inside.

560
00:51:14,012 --> 00:51:16,162
We have new vans also,
but they're just for emergencies.

561
00:51:16,392 --> 00:51:19,963
And the ulcer is not an emergency?
Answer me this, and then I'll get in.

562
00:51:20,309 --> 00:51:22,803
Do you believe
the ulcer is no emergency?

563
00:51:23,340 --> 00:51:26,335
Take your hands off!
Are you blind? Sandu!

564
00:51:26,911 --> 00:51:29,484
Stop fooling around Romica!
Did you expect a helicopter?

565
00:51:30,098 --> 00:51:32,209
Stop that, young man! Nurse!

566
00:51:32,670 --> 00:51:35,702
Come on please, it's late
we need to hurry to the hospital.

567
00:51:37,124 --> 00:51:40,809
Don't put me on that stretcher,
Listen son, I'll sit here.

568
00:51:41,231 --> 00:51:42,883
Yes, sit in this.

569
00:51:43,458 --> 00:51:45,530
- I don't wanna lie on the stretcher.
- I'll help you to the seat.

570
00:51:46,030 --> 00:51:47,757
Come, easy, easy.
There you go.

571
00:51:50,753 --> 00:51:52,750
You don't need to be so rough.

572
00:51:52,980 --> 00:51:55,743
Going to the hospital is not easy,
we all get old.

573
00:51:57,048 --> 00:51:58,737
I just told him to sit there quietly.

574
00:52:00,465 --> 00:52:01,693
Watch that leg.

575
00:52:04,266 --> 00:52:08,106
I forgot to give you the bag.
Here are your pajama and the slippers.

576
00:52:08,911 --> 00:52:11,483
- What am I doing here Sandu?
- Don't worry, Mr. engineer.

577
00:52:11,790 --> 00:52:14,401
They won't keep you in the hospital.
Be good there.

578
00:52:15,399 --> 00:52:17,089
<i>C'mon dear, I'm freezing here.</i>

579
00:52:22,656 --> 00:52:24,499
To the ER at St Spiridon.

580
00:52:25,420 --> 00:52:28,030
- If you stay there, stay put.
- I'm sitting here nicely.

581
00:52:43,579 --> 00:52:46,573
It's not nice to push people
like that. It's not, you know.

582
00:52:48,185 --> 00:52:50,490
Wouldn't you sit a bit further?
Your breath kind of stinks.

583
00:52:51,334 --> 00:52:53,945
I understand you're doing your duty
but not that tough.

584
00:52:54,521 --> 00:52:56,978
We're only
a bunch of miserable people, Mr.

585
00:52:57,476 --> 00:52:59,511
Let him drive, sit there nicely.

586
00:53:05,155 --> 00:53:06,730
How are you feeling?

587
00:53:10,108 --> 00:53:13,447
You know how much
I love those cats of mine?

588
00:53:14,829 --> 00:53:18,285
My heart shrinks,
now that I left them home.

589
00:53:20,205 --> 00:53:21,894
Of course I understand.

590
00:53:31,108 --> 00:53:34,639
- Are you still feeling noxious?
- I feel a kind of sadness, miss.

591
00:53:39,363 --> 00:53:41,013
Course I understand,

592
00:53:41,474 --> 00:53:45,312
my sister has a teckel
and she feels the same way you do.

593
00:53:49,075 --> 00:53:52,838
Excuse me miss,
do you have a cigarette?

594
00:53:53,721 --> 00:53:57,060
Sit there nicely.
We'll get to the hospital right away.

595
00:53:58,443 --> 00:54:01,206
- You can't smoke in here.
- I would like to smoke a cigarette.

596
00:54:01,936 --> 00:54:04,163
You can't smoke in the car,
did you hear?

597
00:54:05,699 --> 00:54:07,618
We'll get to the hospital right away.

598
00:54:11,496 --> 00:54:13,761
Look, I'm not smoking either,
and I actually smoke.

599
00:54:14,682 --> 00:54:17,062
I smoke for about 30 years now.

600
00:54:19,904 --> 00:54:23,474
What did my sister say,
when is she coming?

601
00:54:24,933 --> 00:54:28,351
She said shell be in Bucharest
tomorrow morning by 6 am.

602
00:54:31,191 --> 00:54:37,832
Sorry ma'am, but you don't realize
how hard it is to raise a child.

603
00:54:40,635 --> 00:54:41,749
Do you have children?

604
00:54:42,287 --> 00:54:47,046
I only have one child. A girl, Bianca.
Married in Toronto, Canada.

605
00:54:47,544 --> 00:54:49,004
How interesting.

606
00:54:50,156 --> 00:54:52,038
Torino's in Italy, pops.

607
00:55:00,407 --> 00:55:03,401
- The cold got into me.
- Yeah, it's cold.

608
00:55:04,745 --> 00:55:11,464
My sister has none. We were two.
A boy and a sister.

609
00:55:12,807 --> 00:55:16,071
Actually, it's the other way around,
cause she's the elder. I'm the youngster.

610
00:55:16,915 --> 00:55:19,180
I have a sister too,
younger than me.

611
00:55:20,408 --> 00:55:22,712
And you, Leo?
You are two brothers, right?

612
00:55:23,172 --> 00:55:25,630
Two. Me and Relu, from Germany.

613
00:55:31,160 --> 00:55:34,230
Sorry ma'am,
but I have a terrible headache

614
00:55:34,613 --> 00:55:37,800
and I would lie down a bit, over here.
Is it possible?

615
00:55:39,720 --> 00:55:43,789
- What do you say, your head aches?
- Do you think it's from the ulcer?

616
00:55:44,979 --> 00:55:48,704
This headache, I mean.
And I haven't eaten anything, either.

617
00:55:49,126 --> 00:55:51,276
It is psychosomatic Mr. Lazarescu.

618
00:55:51,583 --> 00:55:54,309
Relax, you're not in pain.
I gave you 2 painkillers.

619
00:55:57,725 --> 00:56:01,066
Listen son, may I lie down a little
on this seat, in the back?

620
00:56:02,218 --> 00:56:04,522
- Do you mind?
- You mean on the stretcher?

621
00:56:05,059 --> 00:56:08,092
- Yes.
- Of course, lie down. Stop the car.

622
00:56:10,740 --> 00:56:12,583
Be patient Mr. Lazarescu,
take it easy.

623
00:56:16,499 --> 00:56:20,299
Mr. Lazarescu, we're here now.
Come on, easy, get up.

624
00:56:23,408 --> 00:56:26,902
- Come on pops, give me your hand.
- Watch out.

625
00:56:31,089 --> 00:56:33,736
Can you walk,
or should we use the stretcher?

626
00:56:34,198 --> 00:56:37,116
- Should I bring a wheelchair?
- Give me the bag.

627
00:56:38,574 --> 00:56:40,648
Come on, go get that wheelchair already.

628
00:56:49,247 --> 00:56:50,707
What, does your leg hurt?

629
00:56:51,052 --> 00:56:53,354
- My right kidney hurts.
- Give me your ID card, please.

630
00:56:59,919 --> 00:57:01,571
Come on, help me take him out.

631
00:57:04,182 --> 00:57:06,869
- Come on.
- Easy, easy now.

632
00:57:11,207 --> 00:57:14,086
The leg.
Hold on.

633
00:57:30,288 --> 00:57:32,168
Can you let us pass, please?

634
00:57:42,227 --> 00:57:43,648
Ok miss, drop your panties.

635
00:57:49,253 --> 00:57:50,674
Here you are.

636
00:57:52,056 --> 00:57:53,861
Abdominal colic and cephalgia.

637
00:57:54,283 --> 00:57:57,507
I'd rather think he has a colon tumor.
I palpated his abdomen, and it's hard.

638
00:57:58,044 --> 00:58:00,348
- No joking?
- What should I do with him, doctor?

639
00:58:01,922 --> 00:58:04,418
Put him in my lap.
Take him over there.

640
00:58:10,446 --> 00:58:13,593
Excuse me, doctor...

641
00:58:19,237 --> 00:58:22,346
Why did they bring him here?
Why not to Fundeni Hospital?

642
00:58:25,802 --> 00:58:27,453
Why didn't you take him to Fundeni?

643
00:58:27,759 --> 00:58:30,831
He should be diagnosed by a specialist
I am not qualified to diagnose.

644
00:58:31,330 --> 00:58:34,094
Well I see you were. Didn't you say
something about his colon?

645
00:58:34,862 --> 00:58:37,243
Get undress, please.
Come on, check his blood pressure

646
00:58:44,651 --> 00:58:46,264
Help the gentleman undress.

647
00:58:53,560 --> 00:58:56,439
Is your belly still sore?
Is it sore right now?

648
00:58:57,168 --> 00:58:58,204
Yes.

649
00:58:59,086 --> 00:59:02,312
Flex your leg.
And the other one. Like that.

650
00:59:03,733 --> 00:59:05,998
The belt, head to the left.

651
00:59:14,329 --> 00:59:15,595
Does it hurt here?

652
00:59:15,941 --> 00:59:19,244
It doesn't hurt there. To be honest,
it's my head that's sore now.

653
00:59:19,781 --> 00:59:20,701
Exhale.

654
00:59:21,776 --> 00:59:23,504
You've drunk a fair bit.

655
00:59:36,749 --> 00:59:39,322
<i>Raluca,
write the lady a prescription.</i>

656
00:59:49,304 --> 00:59:53,297
- Doctor, could it be from my colitis?
- I thought I was the doctor here.

657
00:59:54,717 --> 00:59:59,056
Hey, hey, what's this?
Behave, or you'll get me angry.

658
00:59:59,516 --> 01:00:01,282
Take your prescription and go home.

659
01:00:01,819 --> 01:00:05,274
Doctor,
what should we do with this one?

660
01:00:06,311 --> 01:00:08,038
Keep him or send him
to Panduri Hospital?

661
01:00:08,268 --> 01:00:09,728
- Did you give him Papaverine?
- Yes.

662
01:00:09,920 --> 01:00:11,493
- And the ultrasound?
- I'll do it now.

663
01:00:13,107 --> 01:00:16,524
- Get out of my way! How is it?
- He's been drinking.

664
01:00:17,253 --> 01:00:19,710
Ah! This, we don't like.

665
01:00:20,899 --> 01:00:23,050
Have you celebrated something?

666
01:00:23,357 --> 01:00:25,584
Or do you drink
just for the sake of it?

667
01:00:26,659 --> 01:00:28,233
- Is it you that brought him?
- Yes.

668
01:00:28,616 --> 01:00:30,191
Why here and not to Fundeni Hospital?

669
01:00:31,956 --> 01:00:35,565
Say pops,
has a colon specialist seen you?

670
01:00:36,179 --> 01:00:39,290
Doctor,
I had ulcer surgery, 14 years ago.

671
01:00:43,168 --> 01:00:45,778
And why do you drink,
if you had ulcer?

672
01:00:46,853 --> 01:00:50,538
Look at the zipper he got,
but he doesn't care.

673
01:00:51,843 --> 01:00:53,686
- Do you smoke?
- Yes!

674
01:00:54,492 --> 01:00:56,028
Good, keep it up!

675
01:01:00,981 --> 01:01:04,628
Nothing.
Have you ever had a colonoscopy?

676
01:01:06,240 --> 01:01:09,234
I have problems with my stomach,
I have ulcer.

677
01:01:09,580 --> 01:01:12,613
No pops,
you have problems with your head.

678
01:01:13,650 --> 01:01:15,724
- Maybe it's his colon.
- Ouch.

679
01:01:16,683 --> 01:01:20,636
It hurts, doesn't it?
Have you seen the size of his liver?

680
01:01:21,789 --> 01:01:24,898
One day your liver will burst
from the drink. You hear?

681
01:01:26,665 --> 01:01:28,815
And since when do you diagnose?

682
01:01:29,237 --> 01:01:32,078
Do you have a secret method
I'm not aware of?

683
01:01:32,500 --> 01:01:35,572
Are you using bio-energy?
Can you see the Holy-Spirit?

684
01:01:36,148 --> 01:01:37,605
Cat got your tongue?

685
01:01:37,874 --> 01:01:40,984
- I only said it could be the colon.
- Great, now teach us our trade.

686
01:01:41,638 --> 01:01:44,669
Why did you bring him here?
The hallway is full of his kind.

687
01:01:45,592 --> 01:01:50,429
This is how we got in this shit,
by minding other people's business.

688
01:01:50,852 --> 01:01:54,921
- Doctor, my head hurts.
- Then why do you drink?

689
01:01:55,459 --> 01:01:57,531
Stop drinking
if you don't want to hurt.

690
01:01:57,876 --> 01:02:00,103
- It's been hurting since this morning.
- Then don't drink in the evening.

691
01:02:00,411 --> 01:02:02,715
- Please don't talk to me like that.
- Be quiet.

692
01:02:03,751 --> 01:02:05,556
- I don't think I've heard you right.
- Please, be quiet.

693
01:02:05,863 --> 01:02:08,626
Have you no shame?
Whom do you think you're talking to?

694
01:02:11,044 --> 01:02:13,886
I'll blow you to bits
along with your ulcer.

695
01:02:14,577 --> 01:02:16,497
You pour the drink down your throat,

696
01:02:16,727 --> 01:02:18,993
and then you come to me,
to get you fixed.

697
01:02:19,300 --> 01:02:22,294
A whole team looks after your ass
and operates your ulcer

698
01:02:22,601 --> 01:02:25,404
and you go home and get wrecked.

699
01:02:25,903 --> 01:02:29,051
Did I cause you this?
This ulcer, did I cause it?

700
01:02:30,280 --> 01:02:32,391
The hospitals are full
of people like you

701
01:02:32,698 --> 01:02:36,000
that soak their brains in alcohol
and batter their wives and kids.

702
01:02:37,612 --> 01:02:40,261
Close that door, will you?
Do you take this for a disco?

703
01:02:44,830 --> 01:02:47,478
What are you doing here?
Why are you barging in?

704
01:02:48,631 --> 01:02:51,511
- Please be still, the exam isn't over.
- Stop talking so much.

705
01:02:51,933 --> 01:02:55,119
- I have never beaten my child.
- Alright, but don't get dressed.

706
01:02:55,809 --> 01:02:58,727
Why don't you stay here?
What now, do I have to send for you?

707
01:02:59,457 --> 01:03:01,031
What's all this fuss about?

708
01:03:01,300 --> 01:03:04,487
If you don't keep quiet
I'll throw you all out.

709
01:03:11,550 --> 01:03:13,777
How long does it take you
for a prescription?

710
01:03:14,160 --> 01:03:16,848
- Don't get me started on you, too.
- Sign here.

711
01:03:19,575 --> 01:03:21,149
I'm sorry, you were busy.

712
01:03:24,528 --> 01:03:26,753
Look what you've brought here.

713
01:03:27,483 --> 01:03:30,477
Why did you get dressed? Are you cold?
Lie down over there, I'm not over.

714
01:03:32,089 --> 01:03:34,432
And you're mocking
the other patients as well

715
01:03:34,662 --> 01:03:37,234
those with serious problems,
like that one.

716
01:03:39,922 --> 01:03:43,454
Silvia, give him glucose.
Did you give him anything?

717
01:03:43,798 --> 01:03:47,023
- I gave him the same, plus a painkiller.
- Put an analgesic and some vitamins too.

718
01:03:48,637 --> 01:03:50,749
Make space. Move over.

719
01:03:51,286 --> 01:03:53,398
- What is it?
- Two seriously injured.

720
01:03:54,051 --> 01:03:58,695
Patient, 20 years, craniocerebral
injury. Blood pressure 14 over 9.

721
01:03:59,501 --> 01:04:01,037
Take a look, doctor.

722
01:04:01,959 --> 01:04:05,376
Silvia, call for dr. Kelemen
and dr. Tutui. And quick.

723
01:04:08,332 --> 01:04:10,789
What's your name?
Can you speak?

724
01:04:22,536 --> 01:04:25,109
- How is he?
- Left anisocoria.

725
01:04:28,642 --> 01:04:30,099
Call the tomograph.

726
01:04:31,788 --> 01:04:35,589
- Where did this tragedy happen?
- You mean those? At Saftica.

727
01:04:39,736 --> 01:04:41,503
I think there are at least 20 dead.

728
01:04:43,038 --> 01:04:45,149
- I have to go. Good evening, madam.
- Bye.

729
01:04:46,223 --> 01:04:47,452
Move.

730
01:04:55,439 --> 01:04:58,049
How are you feeling?
Does your head still hurt?

731
01:04:59,085 --> 01:05:00,660
Stay still, don't move.

732
01:05:15,210 --> 01:05:18,358
- Doctor, my head hurts.
- Very well, it means you have one.

733
01:05:20,124 --> 01:05:23,311
Did you take a good look at those
who came? Those are emergencies.

734
01:05:24,385 --> 01:05:26,690
- Doctor, would you come for a minute?
- Wait a second, dear.

735
01:05:27,841 --> 01:05:29,645
Did you throw up blood?
Do you have melena?

736
01:05:30,491 --> 01:05:32,677
- No, I have diarrhea.
- I didn't ask you that.

737
01:05:33,330 --> 01:05:34,597
Raise your hands.

738
01:05:37,861 --> 01:05:40,011
Bullshit, you're ok. Stop drinking.

739
01:05:42,660 --> 01:05:45,923
You don't give a shit about the others.
And I'm supposed to take care of you.

740
01:05:46,615 --> 01:05:48,188
Where's that record?
Give it to me.

741
01:05:48,802 --> 01:05:50,799
It's your duty,
that's why you're paid.

742
01:05:52,142 --> 01:05:57,402
What? My duty? Did I put
the bottle in your hand, you pig?

743
01:05:58,976 --> 01:06:00,743
Did I take you drinking?

744
01:06:01,165 --> 01:06:05,119
- Who told you that we are well paid?
- Why did they bring you on the stretcher?

745
01:06:06,540 --> 01:06:09,495
Why, if you can use your own legs?
Stand up and walk if you can.

746
01:06:10,110 --> 01:06:13,489
I don't need your help.
I can make it alone.

747
01:06:18,019 --> 01:06:20,206
- Look at him.
- Easy, Mr. Lazarescu.

748
01:06:21,319 --> 01:06:24,583
And you were lecturing us.
See what alcohol made of you?

749
01:06:25,197 --> 01:06:29,152
- Are you hurt, Mr. Lazarescu?
- Girl, call someone to take him away.

750
01:06:31,762 --> 01:06:33,375
Costica!

751
01:06:35,908 --> 01:06:36,907
You'd better get dressed.

752
01:06:43,779 --> 01:06:46,083
- Get him out of my sight.
- Doctor?

753
01:06:46,851 --> 01:06:48,309
There's nothing wrong
on the ultrasound.

754
01:06:48,578 --> 01:06:50,345
Some kidney sand,
but within normal values.

755
01:06:50,575 --> 01:06:51,841
- Did you write his prescription?
- Yes,

756
01:06:52,532 --> 01:06:54,299
Then send him home,
what are you waiting for?

757
01:07:18,946 --> 01:07:21,019
His liver
is as big as the Parliament House,

758
01:07:21,211 --> 01:07:23,053
you should take him
to Fundeni Hospital.

759
01:07:23,553 --> 01:07:25,126
I don't think it's hepatitis.

760
01:07:26,279 --> 01:07:29,888
No, you better take him to Floreasca
Hospital or Universitar Hospital.

761
01:07:30,272 --> 01:07:32,306
He needs a liver CT scan.

762
01:07:35,224 --> 01:07:38,371
I would have kept him here,
but you see how crowded it is.

763
01:07:41,328 --> 01:07:42,826
Hurry up with the chair.

764
01:07:44,399 --> 01:07:45,667
Easy.

765
01:07:52,655 --> 01:07:55,993
- You need help?
- No, it's ok. Easy.

766
01:07:59,180 --> 01:08:00,946
Are you comfortable?
Stay there.

767
01:08:02,444 --> 01:08:04,248
Watch your head,
I'm closing the stall.

768
01:08:07,320 --> 01:08:08,356
So?

769
01:08:08,663 --> 01:08:10,889
So we took out those two,
but they are working hard over there.

770
01:08:11,158 --> 01:08:13,769
I don't think there's anyone else left
to rescue in that wreckage.

771
01:08:14,690 --> 01:08:16,764
And they've blocked the road, too.

772
01:08:17,109 --> 01:08:19,298
Didn't you say
they crashed at the exit for Snagov?

773
01:08:19,566 --> 01:08:21,831
No bro, it happened
on the bridge at Saftica.

774
01:08:22,177 --> 01:08:24,173
It had no reason
to make a right for Snagov.

775
01:08:25,133 --> 01:08:26,822
They broke the side barriers, too.

776
01:08:27,129 --> 01:08:29,894
Half of our cars are there.
And there were kids in there.

777
01:08:30,623 --> 01:08:31,967
- Good evening Mrs. Mioara.
- Hi Misu.

778
01:08:32,888 --> 01:08:34,922
They knocked me dead
with their lectures.

779
01:08:35,153 --> 01:08:38,109
And our tipsy grandpa
can't keep his mouth shut.

780
01:08:38,801 --> 01:08:41,795
- What about the accident?
- Well what about it?

781
01:08:42,525 --> 01:08:45,672
They were heading for Brasov, and
they crashed on the bridge, at Saftica.

782
01:08:46,402 --> 01:08:49,474
Probably a blow up on a front tire.
I think they had more than 100 km/hour.

783
01:08:50,088 --> 01:08:52,277
Poor souls, they were going on holiday.

784
01:08:52,507 --> 01:08:54,580
I don't know.
I guess half of them are dead.

785
01:08:54,849 --> 01:08:57,688
We were the third on the scene,
and we got the last ones alive.

786
01:08:58,764 --> 01:09:01,221
- See how life is?
- What about yours?

787
01:09:01,759 --> 01:09:05,138
I don't know, cirrhosis suspicion.
At least that's what dr. Ardelean said.

788
01:09:05,560 --> 01:09:07,977
Isn't he the one involved
in the medicines scandal?

789
01:09:08,439 --> 01:09:11,164
No, that one's name is Aldea, I say.
Sandu Aldea.

790
01:09:11,472 --> 01:09:13,851
I thought his name was Ardelean.

791
01:09:14,159 --> 01:09:16,808
- We're going to Universitar Hospital.
- To do what? The place is swamped.

792
01:09:17,307 --> 01:09:19,036
Most of the casualties went there.

793
01:09:19,418 --> 01:09:21,184
We're going for a CT scan.
Move over.

794
01:09:22,912 --> 01:09:26,368
If you were there to hear the folks
moaning under that bus...

795
01:09:27,750 --> 01:09:29,401
Be still, Mr. Lazarescu.

796
01:09:30,015 --> 01:09:31,896
We're taking you to Universitar
to run full tests.

797
01:09:34,429 --> 01:09:35,467
Let's go.

798
01:09:37,731 --> 01:09:39,959
- Bye, Misu.
- Good bye, ma'am. Take it easy.

799
01:09:41,033 --> 01:09:43,605
Listen, be careful with Leo,
he's a stud.

800
01:09:46,715 --> 01:09:50,324
My gall hurts,
and I have no pills on me.

801
01:09:52,666 --> 01:09:56,351
- Did you try marigold tea?
- Slow down, please slow down.

802
01:09:57,465 --> 01:09:59,231
What happened, Mr. Lazarescu?

803
01:10:00,919 --> 01:10:03,185
Don't take me home girl,
I feel really bad.

804
01:10:03,876 --> 01:10:07,946
My name is Mioara, Mr. Lazarescu.
And his name is Leonard.

805
01:10:08,598 --> 01:10:13,820
Yeah, beautiful... Listen, somebody
take me to the hospital, I'm sick.

806
01:10:15,663 --> 01:10:17,890
Relax, we're on our way
to the hospital.

807
01:10:18,542 --> 01:10:19,770
- Mrs. Mioara.
- Yes?

808
01:10:20,307 --> 01:10:24,070
I feel my head splitting from the pain.
Please take me to the hospital.

809
01:10:24,647 --> 01:10:26,643
We're heading there, I've told you.

810
01:10:28,601 --> 01:10:31,021
Come on Mr. Lazarescu,
don't be a baby.

811
01:10:31,940 --> 01:10:34,628
My sister will be
nice to you, when she'll come.

812
01:10:35,357 --> 01:10:37,545
Never mind your sister, ok?

813
01:10:40,003 --> 01:10:42,307
Look, pops we're almost there.

814
01:10:42,768 --> 01:10:45,877
In 5 minutes we'll be there.
Look, we are near the Parliament House.

815
01:10:48,065 --> 01:10:51,329
I am sorry I caused you trouble
at the hospital.

816
01:10:51,828 --> 01:10:52,710
What do you say?

817
01:10:53,094 --> 01:10:55,589
I am sorry I caused trouble
with the doctors.

818
01:10:55,973 --> 01:10:58,239
Forget about it, we're used to it.

819
01:10:59,045 --> 01:11:02,616
But, at Universitar,
try to be more careful.

820
01:11:03,229 --> 01:11:05,725
They might be less patient.

821
01:11:06,071 --> 01:11:09,026
Yes, you're right,
I lost my temper, I'm sorry.

822
01:11:10,140 --> 01:11:14,172
I know, but you realize that you've
drunk and they might send you home.

823
01:11:14,978 --> 01:11:18,932
That's true, but isn't the doctor's
duty to take care of the patient?

824
01:11:19,699 --> 01:11:21,696
Yeah?
And what is the patient's duty?

825
01:11:23,385 --> 01:11:25,267
I mean, I'm driving you
with the Ambulance,

826
01:11:25,497 --> 01:11:27,302
but shouldn't you behave?

827
01:11:31,448 --> 01:11:34,251
See? He's quiet now.

828
01:11:38,128 --> 01:11:42,006
Pull over, pull over. He threw up.

829
01:11:42,773 --> 01:11:44,539
Wait, we're in the middle
of the junction.

830
01:12:00,472 --> 01:12:04,043
What have you done here?
Give me the napkins.

831
01:12:05,617 --> 01:12:08,879
See, if you don't stay still?
Look what you've done here.

832
01:12:11,797 --> 01:12:14,562
Hold it to your mouth.
Ok. Drive on.

833
01:12:16,289 --> 01:12:17,518
Is it ok?

834
01:12:39,170 --> 01:12:42,894
Excuse me, nurse,
do you have children?

835
01:12:43,969 --> 01:12:46,042
- What did you say?
- Do you have children?

836
01:12:46,772 --> 01:12:49,421
Oh, God, you like to chat.
Yes I have a son and a daughter.

837
01:12:50,420 --> 01:12:53,644
The girl is 18, and the boy 27.
What else?

838
01:12:55,102 --> 01:12:57,368
- Big, you have big kids.
- Yes,

839
01:12:58,673 --> 01:13:04,049
- Excuse me, nurse, but how old are you?
- I'm not that young anymore. I'm 55.

840
01:13:05,162 --> 01:13:07,734
- 55?
- Yes 55, in September.

841
01:13:08,884 --> 01:13:11,879
In September? Just like Virgil,
my brother in law,

842
01:13:12,340 --> 01:13:15,374
only that he is 68.
When in September?

843
01:13:16,256 --> 01:13:21,516
- Dear me, On 1st September.
- He is on 21st or 27th.

844
01:13:46,433 --> 01:13:48,275
Come on pops, we reached the hotel.

845
01:13:49,388 --> 01:13:53,421
For Trauma Center? From the accident?
Are you from the accident in Saftica?

846
01:13:54,073 --> 01:13:57,489
- We're with another case.
- We've been sent for some tests.

847
01:13:58,218 --> 01:14:01,251
So, if you're not from the accident,
go somewhere else, we're crowded.

848
01:14:01,827 --> 01:14:04,630
We've been sent from St. Spiridon
for tests.

849
01:14:04,976 --> 01:14:07,740
Listen, woman, there's no one
to take care of you. Understand?

850
01:14:08,315 --> 01:14:09,391
Really.

851
01:14:09,737 --> 01:14:12,307
Have I told you to take him out?
Put him back and move away.

852
01:14:13,230 --> 01:14:14,765
Why are you following me?

853
01:14:15,878 --> 01:14:17,338
You have a customer.

854
01:14:23,174 --> 01:14:25,899
- What do we do?
- We'll wait and see.

855
01:14:29,777 --> 01:14:31,158
Trauma is full.

856
01:14:31,503 --> 01:14:33,116
There's no room at the 1st,
no room at the 2nd,

857
01:14:33,308 --> 01:14:35,881
no room at mom's, no room at dad's.
Please go away.

858
01:14:36,188 --> 01:14:38,184
We're not staying, we're on our way
to Fundeni Hospital.

859
01:14:38,338 --> 01:14:41,947
Then go to Fundeni.
Am I not clear enough?

860
01:14:42,716 --> 01:14:45,324
We're not for Trauma,
we need to do a CT scan.

861
01:14:45,786 --> 01:14:48,358
What CT scan lady?
Give me that record.

862
01:14:54,770 --> 01:14:56,382
What am I supposed to do now?

863
01:15:01,180 --> 01:15:02,947
You, come here.

864
01:15:07,361 --> 01:15:10,894
Take this one to General Care.
Come on Mr. Driver, time flies.

865
01:15:12,237 --> 01:15:13,505
Out with him, quick.

866
01:15:13,774 --> 01:15:17,075
Move this car quickly, will you?
And please clean the puke.

867
01:15:17,689 --> 01:15:18,918
Now blame it on me.

868
01:15:20,261 --> 01:15:21,605
Slowly.

869
01:15:22,450 --> 01:15:24,369
Hold on pops, don't wiggle.

870
01:15:31,739 --> 01:15:34,082
Move away.

871
01:16:01,417 --> 01:16:04,757
Could you let us pass? Thanks.

872
01:16:06,945 --> 01:16:08,250
Easy.

873
01:16:10,401 --> 01:16:12,283
<i>- Wait outside, please.
- For a hemogram.</i>

874
01:16:22,341 --> 01:16:23,454
I'll wait here, in the hall.

875
01:16:41,921 --> 01:16:42,918
Leo.

876
01:16:58,199 --> 01:17:00,425
- Why don't you go in?
- She told me to wait.

877
01:17:01,231 --> 01:17:03,727
You may go in, lady,
I see you have an emergency.

878
01:17:04,457 --> 01:17:07,373
- I say we let the lady first.
- Of course, madam, go in.

879
01:17:32,329 --> 01:17:33,672
Come in.

880
01:17:45,036 --> 01:17:48,837
- How do you feel, Mr. Remus?
- My head hurts, my temples...

881
01:17:50,834 --> 01:17:54,288
And the booze, why did you drink it?
Get him inside.

882
01:18:06,613 --> 01:18:09,145
- Can you walk, just two steps?
- I try.

883
01:18:20,778 --> 01:18:23,159
Sit here.

884
01:18:29,033 --> 01:18:30,569
I'll be here, by the benches.

885
01:18:31,643 --> 01:18:33,217
Look at me.

886
01:18:34,600 --> 01:18:36,097
I don't like what I see.

887
01:18:36,558 --> 01:18:39,821
- I throw up morning.
- What? You throw up in the morning?

888
01:18:40,320 --> 01:18:41,894
No, since morning.

889
01:18:43,390 --> 01:18:44,850
We'll see in an instant.

890
01:18:46,462 --> 01:18:49,035
But first,
we'll take some blood for tests.

891
01:18:50,417 --> 01:18:53,412
Help him undress.
Please sit.

892
01:18:55,868 --> 01:18:57,865
Did you sign in
the one from the Ambulance?

893
01:18:58,172 --> 01:19:00,475
Then come and get the hemogram,
proteins and transaminases.

894
01:19:01,205 --> 01:19:03,970
- And put him a venous catheter.
- He needs a CT scan, doctor.

895
01:19:04,891 --> 01:19:06,120
The vest, too.

896
01:19:13,183 --> 01:19:14,259
Are you coming?

897
01:19:15,871 --> 01:19:18,788
And look,
you have an ulcer surgery.

898
01:19:19,901 --> 01:19:21,015
May I?

899
01:19:23,780 --> 01:19:26,122
I'll use also this arm.

900
01:19:43,358 --> 01:19:46,622
Ah, this drink.
You never have enough of it!

901
01:19:47,275 --> 01:19:49,655
Why do you drink
if you have an ulcer surgery?

902
01:19:51,153 --> 01:19:53,264
Did you take him enough blood?
I want a ionogram, too.

903
01:19:59,636 --> 01:20:02,017
Come on, flex your legs.

904
01:20:04,667 --> 01:20:06,816
- What? The right one is slower?
- Yes.

905
01:20:07,354 --> 01:20:08,582
Head aside.

906
01:20:12,959 --> 01:20:15,531
- Nothing here.
- Doesn't affect me drinking.

907
01:20:15,876 --> 01:20:18,411
- What did you say?
- Sometimes doesn't affect.

908
01:20:19,293 --> 01:20:21,712
I don't understand.
Who is not affecting you?

909
01:20:22,403 --> 01:20:24,746
I palpated him at home,
and his abdomen was hard.

910
01:20:25,168 --> 01:20:26,819
I thought it's the colon.

911
01:20:31,732 --> 01:20:34,036
It's not the colon, it's the liver.

912
01:20:34,765 --> 01:20:37,108
Look at his color,
the liver is the problem.

913
01:20:37,645 --> 01:20:39,411
- Did you throw up with blood?
- No ma'am.

914
01:20:43,558 --> 01:20:46,052
- It hurts here, doesn't it?
- Don't get close.

915
01:20:46,974 --> 01:20:50,046
What about black stool?
You know, melena.

916
01:20:51,620 --> 01:20:55,228
- I say a things you don't want to get.
- No kidding.

917
01:20:55,957 --> 01:20:58,031
Do you have melena?
Yes or no?

918
